.El
.Ss Controllers
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fn rk_controller_create_with_view "rk_view *view" "const char *title"
A controller around a view; takes
.Fa view .
.Fn rk_controller_create
takes a class whose
.Fa load
builds the view when it is first needed.
.It Fn rk_places "rk_controller *home"
A navigation stack starting at
.Fa home .
.Fn rk_places_go
turns the current place away and the new one in;
.Fn rk_places_back ,
Escape or the back button turn back, and
.Fn rk_places_on_back
hears it.
.It Fn rk_panorama , Fn rk_panorama_add
One place laid out sideways in sections under a strip of their titles.
.Fn rk_panorama_insert ,
.Fn rk_panorama_remove ,
.Fn rk_panorama_set_title
and
.Fn rk_panorama_set_width
change a section where it stands.
.It Fn rk_pivot , Fn rk_pivot_add "rk_controller *pivot" "const char *title" "rk_view *page" , Fn rk_pivot_select
Facets of one place; the change slides from its side.
.Fn rk_pivot_add_controller
adds a facet that is a controller, under its title, which may change;
.Fn rk_pivot_insert_controller
puts one at an index and
.Fn rk_pivot_remove
takes one out, the one before it showing when it was in sight.
.Fn rk_pivot_on_change
hears the user pick a page.
A pivot with no pivot or panorama above it is the window's way between
places: its titles take the nav level, its pages start at their indent, and a
change turns the place as
.Fn rk_places_go
does instead of sliding.
.It Fn rk_pivot_set_layout "rk_controller *pivot" "rk_pivot_layout layout"
.Dv RK_PIVOT_TOP
(the default) lays the titles along the top;
.Dv RK_PIVOT_SIDE
lays them as a list down the leading side, one size, the one in sight stepped
in and dark.
Up and Down then pick the title.
A window narrower than 760 or lower than 481 logical pixels keeps them along
the top.
.It Fn rk_pivot_set_wide "rk_controller *pivot" "float width" , Fn rk_pivot_is_wide
From
.Fa width
up (0: the app's
.Dv RK_PIVOT_WIDE ,
1300 until
.Fn rk_app_set_metric ;
below 0: never) every page shows, side by side as panorama sections three
tiles wide
.Pq a page with a width of its own keeps it ,
space-xl apart, and the strip stays as a jump list.
A title, picked by a click or by Left, Right, Home and End with focus staying
on the strip, glides its page to the leading edge over pivot-glide; Tab goes
into the page chosen; the wheel moves the pages sideways, and the page at the
leading edge becomes the one chosen, unless the chosen one is still whole in
sight.
Narrower, one page at a time again, the one last chosen.
A pivot that picks the place, or with its titles down the side, never goes
wide.
.It Fn rk_controller_embed "rk_controller *owner" "rk_controller *child"
A controller inside another's views, such as a pivot in a page: the owner
takes
.Fa child ,
gives it its window and tells it when it appears and goes.
Returns the child's view as a reference: add it where it goes.
.It Fn rk_controller_present , Fn rk_controller_dismiss
A sheet: a short question from the top edge.
.Fn rk_controller_on_dismiss
hears the user close it.
.It Fn rk_confirm "rk_controller *presenter" "const rk_confirm_desc *desc" "void (*answered)(bool ok, void *user)" "void *user"
A question in a sheet with two answers: the safe one is the primary button
and has focus
.Pf ( Fa desc->cancel_is_safe
for what cannot be undone); Escape and the shading answer cancel.
.Fa answered
hears it once.
Returns the sheet, so the app may dismiss it before the answer.
.El
.Ss Motion
Motion is named by what it means, never by numbers you pick.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fn rk_animate_begin "rk_motion motion" , Fn rk_animate_commit
Changes between the two travel with the motion:
.Dv RK_MOTION_STATE ,
.Dv RK_MOTION_REFLOW
(the layout glides),
.Dv RK_MOTION_ENTER ,
.Dv RK_MOTION_LEAVE ,
.Dv RK_MOTION_MORPH .
.Fn rk_animate_on_done
runs when they have arrived.
.It Fn rk_view_transition "rk_view *view" "rk_transition transition"
Called before a change:
.Dv RK_TRANSITION_PEEK
(a new number peeks in),
.Dv RK_TRANSITION_FLIP
(a new status turns the tile over),
.Dv RK_TRANSITION_CROSSFADE .
.El
.Pp
Under reduced motion every change is instant, never skipped.
.Ss Keys
Whatever takes a press or a key takes focus, and Tab reaches it, a
toast's action last.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Tab , Shift+Tab
Focus in reading order; inside a sheet, its views and the toast.
.It Enter , Space
Press the focused button, tile or row: it sinks, then activates.
.It Escape
Closes the innermost: a menu, a toast with focus, a sheet, then the place.
.It Shift+F10
The focused view's menu.
.It Ctrl+Z , Ctrl+Shift+Z , Ctrl+Y
Undo and redo: a text field's own history inside it, the app's elsewhere.
On macOS, Cmd for Ctrl.
.It Left , Right , Home , End
In a strip of titles, the next, the first or the last.
In a wide pivot focus stays on the strip, and Tab goes into the page chosen.
.It Page Up , Page Down , Home , End
A panorama's sections.
.It Up , Down
The section in sight scrolls, when nothing focused takes the key.
.It F2
In a table, the active row's first editable cell.
.It Up No on a table's first row
Into its head: Left and Right go between columns, Enter or Space sorts,
Ctrl+Left and Ctrl+Right change the width (with Shift, four times as much),
Down or Escape go back to the rows.
.El
.Ss Testing and measuring
These are declared in
.In rekta_test.h ,
apart from what an app needs.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fn rk_view_tap , Fn rk_window_key , Fn rk_window_inject
Input as if it came from the system.
.It Fn rk_window_view_at
What a press at a point reaches.
.It Fn rk_window_snapshot
The window's pixels as a PNG.
.It Fn rk_app_run_for
Without a screen
.Pq Fa desc->headless ,
advances the virtual clock, running every frame.
.It Fn rk_app_stats "rk_stats *stats" , Fn rk_app_stats_reset
Frames drawn, time spent drawing, the slowest frame, input latency,
glyphs rasterized, animations running; the reset starts the counts again.
.El
.Sh RETURN VALUES
Constructors never return
.Dv NULL :
when memory runs out the library says so on standard error and aborts.
Functions that take a reference take it even when they fail, so a caller
never has to release it on an error path.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width RK_PLATFORM
.It Ev RK_PLATFORM
.Li x11
uses X11 even where a Wayland compositor answers.
.It Ev RK_HEADLESS
Non-zero: no screen; windows live in memory and the clock is virtual.
.It Ev RK_SCALE
Device pixels per logical pixel without a screen, and on X11 in place of
.Li Xft.dpi ,
which is otherwise followed while the app runs.
.It Ev RK_THREADS
How many threads draw big layers; 1 draws everything on the main thread.
.It Ev RK_FPS
Frames a second while something moves, instead of the display's rate.
.It Ev RK_HUD
Non-zero: frame time, input latency and animations in the window's corner.
.It Ev RK_TRACE
Non-zero: a line for every frame on standard error.
.It Ev RK_PROFILE
Non-zero: the drawing time when the app ends.
.El
.Sh ICONS
.Fn rk_button_set_icon ,
.Fn rk_icon
and
.Fn rk_canvas_icon
take these names; any other is said
.Pq see Sx ERRORS
and draws nothing:
.Bd -filled -offset indent
archive back bell calendar check chevron-down chevron-left chevron-right
chevron-up clock close copy down download edit error external eye file
filter folder forward grip home info install link lock menu minus more
motion offline pause pin play plus redo refresh search sort stop theme
trash tune undo up upload user warning window
.Ed
.Sh EXAMPLES
A section of tiles, a button that counts, and a tile that opens
something, declared:
.Bd -literal
/* hello.c: a first app. A section of tiles, a button that counts, a tile that opens something. */
#include "rekta.h"

static int finished = 312;                         /* the state: the window shows what is here */

static void build_one(rk_view *button, void *user) { finished++; }   /* the window follows: the new number peeks in */

static void open_notes(rk_view *tile, void *user) {
  rk_window_toast(rk_view_window(tile), "Release notes are on their way.", NULL, NULL, NULL);
}

static void today(void *user) {                    /* what the window shows: built again after every handler */
  RK_PANORAMA() RK_SECTION("today") {
    RK_LABEL("Today", .style = RK_TEXT_GROUP);
    RK_TILES() {
      RK_TILE(rk_ui_fmt("%d", finished), .label = "finished today", .status = RK_STATUS_SUCCESS, .span = { 2, 1 });
      RK_TILE("0.3", .label = "release notes", .on_press = open_notes);   /* it presses, and opens something */
    }
    RK_BUTTON("build one", .on_press = build_one);
  }
}

static void launch(void *user) {
  rk_window_desc desc = { .size = sizeof desc, .title = "My tool", .width = 960, .height = 640, .build = today };
  rk_window_create(&desc);
}

int main(void) {
  rk_app_desc app = { .size = sizeof app, .name = "My tool", .id = "de.example.tool", .launch = launch };
  return rk_app_main(&app);
}
.Ed
.Sh ERRORS
Misuse does nothing and is said through
.Fn rk_app_set_log
.Pq standard error until set :
a setter for one kind of view called on another, a descriptor whose
.Fa size
is 0, a call from a thread other than the main one, an icon that is not
in the set, a pointer that is no Rekta object or one already released.
A domain colour that breaks the rules is set, and said as a warning; a
metric or timing that is the design's, and a word's format without exactly
one
.Li %s ,
are said and not set.
A view added to itself or inside itself asserts in debug builds.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Pa docs/core.md
(the design and the ABI rules),
.Pa include/rekta.h ,
.Pa demo/demo.c
(every feature in one window).
.Sh STANDARDS
C99.
Descriptors that may grow start with
.Vt uint32_t size ;
enums are 32 bits wide; strings are UTF-8 and copied by the library.
.Sh BUGS
Scripts that join or reorder (Arabic, Hebrew, the Indic scripts) are not
shaped.
The accessibility tree is built, but the bridges to the systems' screen
readers (UI Automation, NSAccessibility, AT-SPI) are not there yet.
